# Storage drivers the filesystem PRD needs, built as exact-source modules
# against the DE25's vendor Image (de25-6.12.11-gd7d192a9ddd9.config).
# build-storage-modules.sh merges this into the exact-source output tree.
#
# Only options that leave every built-in object unchanged belong here: a
# module built against a config the Image was not built with must not see a
# different layout of any structure the Image owns.
#
# NOT here: CONFIG_BLK_DEV_SR (sr_mod) and the CONFIG_CDROM it selects.
# include/linux/blkdev.h adds `struct cdrom_device_info *cdi` to struct
# gendisk under IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CDROM), ahead of node_id, bb, diskseq and
# open_mode. The Image was built without it, so cdrom.ko/sr_mod.ko would
# write every later gendisk field 8 bytes off. Optical needs a rebuilt Image.
#
# CONFIG_USB_UAS: the built-in usb-storage was compiled without it, so it
# does not step aside for UAS-capable devices (drivers/usb/storage/usb.c,
# storage_probe) and claims any device with a bulk-only altsetting first.
# uas.ko binds only UAS-only devices until the Image is rebuilt with UAS.

CONFIG_ISO9660_FS=m
CONFIG_JOLIET=y
CONFIG_ZISOFS=y
CONFIG_UDF_FS=m
CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=m
CONFIG_EXFAT_DEFAULT_IOCHARSET="utf8"
CONFIG_NTFS3_FS=m
CONFIG_NLS_UTF8=m
CONFIG_USB_UAS=m
